    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Valid insurance certificate covering the vehicle for the duration of the transit. The certificate should state the policy number, coverage limits, and the insured value. It is advisable to opt for a policy that includes marine transit coverage if the vehicle will be moved by sea.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 04</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">IBA‑approved consignment bilty. The Bilty is a transport receipt issued by the Indian Bulk and Allied (IBA) logistics network. It must contain details such as consignor, consignee, vehicle number, route, and the agreed freight rate.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>In addition to the above, the transport company will strongly recommend that you secure 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance. This type of insurance ensures that the vehicle’s full market value is covered in the event of loss or damage during sea transport.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Unlike standard policies that may offer a percentage of the declared value, 100% coverage eliminates any shortfall, giving you peace of mind that the vehicle’s worth will be fully protected.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The insurance provider will issue a certificate that explicitly states the 100% coverage and the insured value, which should be submitted to the carrier alongside the other documents.</span></li></ul>

<p>Before finalizing the booking, verify that each document is up‑to‑date and matches the vehicle’s details. Keep original copies and provide the carrier with the required photocopies. Proper documentation not only speeds up the loading process but also safeguards your investment throughout the journey.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


